  "result": "All six tests pass.\n\n**What I built:** `wire/codec.py` implements Approach A, a compact binary format. Each encoding is a 9-byte header (magic `WIRE`, version byte, u32 record count), followed by fixed 15-byte packed records (`<IHdB`), and a trailing CRC-32 over everything before it. `decode` rejects bad magic, unsupported versions, any length that doesn't match the declared count, and checksum mismatches, all as `CodecError`. `encode` validates field names, integer types, and ranges before packing.\n\n**Why Approach A:** the schema is fixed-width and fully numeric, so `struct` packing gives exact float round-trips (including NaN and -0.0) for free, and the length-plus-checksum framing makes truncation and corruption detection reliable and cheap. JSON lines would have needed extra care for NaN (not valid JSON) and offered readability the spec didn't ask for.\n\nNothing was committed. Run `python -m pytest -q` from the repo root to reproduce.",
